        <h2><span class="idx">02</span>Who it's for</h2>
        <p class="lead">The Aura X3 is for the commuter, the open-office escapee, and anyone who wants flagship features without the flagship tax. If your budget stops at $100 and your expectations don't, this is your pair.</p>
        <p>It's <strong>not</strong> for runners (no IP rating — get the PulseFit Sport below) or audiophiles chasing planar-magnetic detail. For everyone else, read on.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="liked" class="reveal">
        <h2><span class="idx">03</span>What we liked</h2>
        <p><strong>The battery is absurd.</strong> We ran the X3 down from 100% with ANC on at 75 dB and it lasted 31.2 hours. The category average in our 2026 test pool is 24.6. A 10-minute USB-C top-up bought us a full workday.</p>
        <p><strong>The tuning is grown-up.</strong> No scooped mids, no bass bloat. Acoustic tracks keep their texture, podcasts stay intelligible, and the 8-band EQ (clumsy as the app is) lets you nudge things further.</p>
        <figure>
          <!-- Replace with: images/aura-x3-anc-rig.jpg -->
          <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/anc-test-rig/900/500" alt="Aura X3 mounted on our acoustic measurement rig" loading="lazy" />
